claims.evidence:
Explicit channel map: bioRxiv preprint Fig. 6A (p.52) shows the A375 whole-proteome workflow as Light = DMSO, Heavy = A922500, 72h, then in-gel digestion, QE-HF and MaxQuant. This is the workflow the Cell Rep Fig. 5A legend references ("DMSO n = 3, A922500 n = 3", 114 up-regulated proteins with NRF2/FAO/PPAR themes). Supporting sources: the authors' code names the H/L ratio of these experiments PRO_72h (4_proteinGroupsLT_DJWQC.R:89), the file names encode 0_72, and the PRIDE keywords name A922500 (spelled a229500) and A375. Data check (labeldir_check.txt) on H/L:
- HMOX1 4.7-5.8, NQO1 1.4, SQSTM1 1.7-1.9 and SOD2 1.2-1.3 up;
- CPT1A, ACADVL and ACSL1 1.2-1.5 up;
- PLIN2 0.51-0.54 down (lipid-droplet loss);
- median log2 H/L about 0;
- 111 proteins with mean ratio >1.5 in the authors' table, against 114 in the paper.
This confirms heavy = A922500. The control (DMSO vehicle) is written as untreated per the template example and campaign rule 4. A922500 has no NCIT/EFO term (OLS 0 hits), so it is free text. The concentration (30 uM, paper Compounds section) is not encoded.
